            <ArticleTitle>Extubation of the patient after a difficult intubation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1778-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a difficult intubation in a heavy smoker requiring reoperative coronary artery bypass grafting is presented. A technique is described to extubate patients with marginal pulmonary function and a difficult intubation using airway exchange catheters.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
